Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 09:49:18 -0700
Subject: Prevent crash if WidgetBase is destroyed during GetTextInputType.

During UpdateTextInputState and composition updates, calling
GetTextInputType can result in the destruction of the WidgetBase. This
CL adds WeakPtr checks immediately after GetTextInputType calls to
ensure the widget is still alive before proceeding, preventing potential
use-after-free crashes. A unit test is also added to verify this
behavior.

BUG=553129513

Change-Id: Id77925e08581ef1b1d50f3b8404466e04c083ff3
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8299776
Commit-Queue: Dave Tapuska <dtapuska@chromium.org>
Reviewed-by: Vladimir Levin <vmpstr@chromium.org>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1687328}

Electron adaptation notes (42-x-y):
- widget_base_input_handler_unittest.cc does not exist on this branch; the
  test-only hunk is dropped. widget_base.cc merged unchanged.

